## Abstract

This project focuses on comparing three important Generative AI approaches: Prompt Engineering, Retrieval-Augmented Generation (RAG), and Fine-Tuning for customer support automation. The main objective is to understand how these approaches can be applied to develop intelligent systems capable of answering customer queries accurately and efficiently.

The Prompt Engineering approach will use carefully designed instructions to guide a Large Language Model (LLM) in generating relevant responses. The RAG approach will retrieve relevant information from an external knowledge source and use it as context for generating more accurate and informative answers. The Fine-Tuning approach will explore adapting a pre-trained language model using domain-specific customer support data to improve its performance for a particular task.

The project aims to implement and compare these three approaches based on response accuracy, relevance, response time, reliability, and overall performance. Through this comparison, the study intends to identify the strengths, limitations, and suitable applications of each approach in customer support automation.

## Planned Technology Stack

- **Programming Language:** Python
- **LLM / API:** Google Gemini API
- **Prompting:** Prompt Engineering
- **RAG:** Retrieval-Augmented Generation
- **Fine-Tuning:** Pre-trained Language Model Adaptation
- **Data Processing:** Python Libraries
- **Development Environment:** Visual Studio Code
- **Version Control:** Git and GitHub
- **Documentation:** Markdown

Additional frameworks, libraries, databases, and evaluation tools will be selected and documented during implementation.

